---
import FeatureCard from '@chassis-ui/docs/components/FeatureCard.astro'
---

<section class="home-section py-3xl md:py-6xl">
  <div class="container 2xl section-content py-3xl md:py-6xl">
    <div class="grid mb-3xl md:mb-6xl">
      <header class="section-header col-span-full lg:col-span-10 lg:col-start-2 xl:col-span-8 xl:col-start-3 text-center">
        <h2 class="section-title font-3xl md:font-4xl lg:font-5xl mb-xs md:mb-sm lg:mb-md">
          <span class="font-normal d-block">The Chassis design system,</span> as React components.
        </h2>
        <p class="section-body md:font-lg lg:font-xl m-0">
          Chassis React gives your team the interactive layer of Chassis UI: components that look
          exactly like the CSS framework and the Figma library, behave accessibly out of the box,
          and type-check against the design system.
        </p>
      </header>
    </div>

    <div class="section-features grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-md md:gap-xl">
      <div>
        <FeatureCard icon="cx-css3">
          <Fragment slot="title">Styled by Chassis CSS</Fragment>
          <Fragment slot="body">
            Every component renders the markup and class names of Chassis CSS, so the React output
            matches what the CSS docs and Figma show, and it re-themes with the same tokens.
          </Fragment>
        </FeatureCard>
      </div>
      <div>
        <FeatureCard icon="cx-universal-access">
          <Fragment slot="title">Accessible by Default</Fragment>
          <Fragment slot="body">
            Built on React Aria and React Stately. Keyboard navigation, focus management, ARIA
            semantics and screen reader announcements come with every component, not as an
            afterthought.
          </Fragment>
        </FeatureCard>
      </div>
      <div>
        <FeatureCard icon="cx-brackets-curly">
          <Fragment slot="title">TypeScript First</Fragment>
          <Fragment slot="body">
            Written in strict TypeScript with typed props, polymorphic elements and generic
            collections. Autocomplete carries the design system into the editor.
          </Fragment>
        </FeatureCard>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
